<title>UK: IFC sets 150 bln lire three-year zero-coupon bond.</title>
<headline>IFC sets 150 bln lire three-year zero-coupon bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Cariplo and Citibank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   INTERNATIONAL FINANCE CORP</p>
<p> AMT    150 BLN LIRE  COUPON    *ZERO	MATURITY    14.FEB.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.90    PAY DATE    14.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.50 PCT  REOFFER    99.60     SPREAD	=</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) =	   SALE LIMITS US/UK/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIP     =</p>
<p> NOTES	*REDEMPTION VALUE IS THE HIGHER OF 110 PERCENTOR</p>
<p>		 100 PERCENT PLUS ((MIB I LESS MIB 0) / MIB 0 WHERE</p>
<p>		 MIB 0 IS THE FIVE DAY AVERAGE OF THE MIB30 INDEX</p>
<p>		 FOR 03.FEB.97-07.FEB.97 AND MIB I IS THE MONTHLY</p>
<p>		 AVERAGE OF THE CLOSING MIB30 INDEX FOR THE THIRD</p>
<p>		 BUSINESS FRIDAY OF EACH MONTH STARTING FEBRUARY</p>
<p>		 1997 THROUGH JANUARY 2000.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
